- Own stores/employees (no franchise like Domino’s Pizza Belgium or recruitment agency);

\*\*Ideal\*\*
- HR team is 1 to 5 people;
- Company size between 250 - 5.000;
- Have a location structure;
- Don’t have a good internal communication app;
- Need for more than one component.

\*\*Very ideal\*\*

- Frontline employees are very important to the company succes (sales or service roles);
- No HQ above that owns many parts of the Employee Experience;
- Value great UX;
- Already have a WFM system (preferably with a ugly/ slow app).

\*\*Solution need\*\*
\*\*Internal communication need\*\*
\*\*Need\*\*
- Centralize all internal communication in one platform to effectively communicate with the frontline so they are well informed and engaged.

\*\*Characteristics / pain:\*\*
- 100+ employees for top down communication need;
- 50+ employees per location for store communication need;
- There must be internal communication use case;
- Currently too many different communication channels and (ideally) not used properly;
- Work-life balance is an issue. Don’t want to use consumer apps;
- Employees are not engaged;
- Can’t reach employees effectively so there is a lot of miscommunication and employees are uninformed.

\*\*Onboarding need\*\*
