What is a JavaScript function that can be used to dynamically calculate the macronutrient ratios for a given set of ingredients, taking into account net carbs and fiber? Here's an example of the ingredients and their nutritional values:
| Ingredient | Calories | Fat (g) | Protein (g) | Net Carbs (g) | Fiber (g) |
|------------|----------|---------|-------------|----------------|--------------|
| Salmon     | 233      | 15.0     | 22.0        | 0.0              | 0.0             |
| Avocado   | 160      | 15.0     | 2.0          | 2.0              | 2.0             |
| Almonds   | 163      | 14.0     | 6.0          | 3.0              | 2.0             |
| Olive Oil    | 120      | 14.0     | 0.0          | 0.0              | 0.0             |
| Broccoli   | 55        | 0.5       | 5.0          | 3.5              | 2.6             |
Here is a JavaScript function that takes in an array of ingredients (each with the same format as the table above) and returns the macronutrient ratios as an object:
```javascript
function calculateMacros(ingredients) {
  let totalCalories = 0;
  let totalFat = 0;
  let totalProtein = 0;
  let totalNetCarbs = 0;
  let totalFiber = 0;

  ingredients.forEach((ingredient) => {
    totalCalories += ingredient[1];
    totalFat += ingredient[2];
    totalProtein += ingredient[3];
    totalNetCarbs += ingredient[4];
    totalFiber += ingredient[5];
  });

  const netCarbs = totalNetCarbs - (totalFiber / 2);
  const totalMacros = totalFat + totalProtein + netCarbs;
  const fatRatio = totalFat / totalMacros;
  const proteinRatio = totalProtein / totalMacros;
  const carbRatio = netCarbs / totalMacros;

  return {
    fatRatio,
    proteinRatio,
    carbRatio,
  };
}
```
